1
00:00:04,230 --> 00:00:10,130
The 3D organization of the genome is key in regulating gene expression and cell function.

2
00:00:11,170 --> 00:00:19,020
Genome architecture is shaped by proteins that mediate spatial proximity between genetic elements that may lie thousands of bases apart.

3
00:00:20,290 --> 00:00:24,720
Genome confirmation capture sequencing lets us spy into the genomes architecture.

4
00:00:25,090 --> 00:00:27,500
and reveals how it determines cell behavior

5
00:00:27,940 --> 00:00:32,210
decides between health and disease and how it directs cell differentiation.

6
00:00:33,380 --> 00:00:40,050
Despite its obvious importance, we cannot easily engineer the 3D genome organization up until now.

7
00:00:40,810 --> 00:00:44,300
We, the IGM team Heidelberg, introduce Picasso.

8
00:00:44,870 --> 00:00:50,830
Plasmid Integrated, cast stapled origami, the first toolbox to rationally engineer the 3D genome.

